        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Horton Foote, David Foster Wallace\n- Roles: playwright, screenwriter, writer, university instructor\n- Works: To Kill a Mockingbird, Tender Mercies\n- Topics: Golden Age of Television\n\nFacts:\n- Albert Horton Foote Jr. was born on March 14, 1916, and died on March 4, 2009.\n- Albert Horton Foote Jr. was an American playwright and screenwriter.\n- Albert Horton Foote Jr. was known for writing the screenplay for the 1962 film \"To Kill a Mockingbird.\"\n- Albert Horton Foote Jr. was known for writing the screenplay for the 1983 film \"Tender Mercies.\"\n- Albert Horton Foote Jr. was also known for notable live television dramas during the Golden Age of Television.\n- David Foster Wallace was born on February 21, 1962, and died on September 12, 2008.\n- David Foster Wallace was an American writer and university instructor of English and creative writing.",
